          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 588817295,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> There is definitely a link at the bottom of commit 7dbd4baa211241d640fe878b8f4a8cd5c2a38eaa\n\nThe commit message does not match the merge request message; for example, the commit message has\n\n>     Raw string literals are enclosed with r\"...\" or R\"...\". Double quotes\n>     can be include in the string but they must be escaped with backslash.\n>     In escape sequences backslashes are preserved in the final result.\n>     \n>     So for example the string \"a\\\\\\\"b\" is the same as r\"a\\\"b\".\n>     \n>     r\"\\\\\\a\" is the same as \"\\\\\\\\\\\\a\".\n> \n>     [1]https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#string-and-bytes-literals\n\nwhereas the merge request has\n\n>     Also make the embedded NUL byte synctatically invalid.\n>     \n>     Related with #16156.\n\nDid you change the commit message after creating the merge request?\n\nIf so, your changes to the commit message did *not* get copied over to the merge request, because GitLab doesn't do that - you would have to manually copy them over.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-31T08:46:34.375Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-31T08:47:34.785Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 102026440,
